@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Registrar usuario normal
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Torres",
  "email": "ana@example.com",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

### Login de usuario normal
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@example.com",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

### Extraer token de Ana
@userToken = {{loginUser.response.body.accessToken}}

### Perfil de Ana
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Buscar ciudades cuyo nombre contiene "mad"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities?search=mad
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Listar ciudades con aeropuertos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/with-airports
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Listar aeropuertos de París (id 3 en los datos iniciales)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/3/airports
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Ana, que es usuario normal, no puede crear una ciudad: debe responder 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cities
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Valencia",
  "country": "España"
}

### Login de administración
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@aeropuertos.test",
  "password": "password"
}

### Extraer token de administrador
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### El administrador crea Valencia
# @name createCity
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cities
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Valencia",
  "country": "España"
}

### Extraer id de la ciudad creada
@valenciaId = {{createCity.response.body.id}}

### El administrador añade el aeropuerto de Valencia
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/airports
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "iataCode": "VAC",
  "name": "Aeropuerto de Valencia",
  "cityId": {{valenciaId}}
}

### Filtrar aeropuertos por ciudad
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/airports?cityId={{valenciaId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json


##2 Adam

### El administrador borra Teruel (id 4, sin aeropuertos) --> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/4
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Borrar París (id 3, tiene aeropuertos) --> 409
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Un usuario normal intenta borrar una ciudad --> 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/4
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Borrar una ciudad que no existe --> 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}




## 1 carlos

### Ver la ciudad con id 1 (debe devolver Madrid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Ciudad que no existe: debe responder 404 CITY_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Id con formato incorrecto: debe responder 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json





##4 Adam

### Listar todos los aeropuertos (sin filtros)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/airports
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Buscar aeropuertos cuyo nombre contiene "mad" (debe devolver Madrid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/airports?search=mad
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Buscar aeropuertos por codigo IATA "cdg" (debe devolver Paris-Charles de Gaulle)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/airports?search=cdg
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Buscar aeropuertos combinando search "par" y cityId 3 (solo los de Paris que coinciden)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/airports?search=par&cityId=3
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json


##6 Adam

### Listar todos los usuarios como administrador (debe responder 200 sin password_hash)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Un usuario normal intenta listar los usuarios (debe responder 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Listar usuarios sin token (debe responder 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Accept: application/json


## 7 Carlos

### El administrador convierte a Ana en admin --> 200 con role "admin"
# Cambia el 2 por el id de Ana (lo ves en GET /api/users)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "role": "admin"
}

### Devolver a Ana al rol user --> 200 con role "user"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "role": "user"
}

### Rol que no existe --> 422
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "role": "superadmin"
}

### Sin rol en el body --> 422
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

### El administrador intenta quitarse su propio rol (id 1) --> 409
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "role": "user"
}

### Un usuario normal intenta cambiar un rol --> 403
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/2/role
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "role": "admin"
}

### Usuario que no existe --> 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/9999/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "role": "user"
}